<page type="text" lines="ocr">
  <layout>One column of verse, set in roman and italic with small capitals. Below the last line, at the right edge, a catchword is cut off. No running head, page number or signature is printed. Faint show-through in the right margin is not transcribed.</layout>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Vetus</i> PARENTIS : <i>quaque puris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Rebus ament hilarare pectus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Hic namque</i> ABRAMI <i>conspicitur</i> FIDES</l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Inuicta cunctis casibus, &amp; potens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Tentationis luctuosa</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Non solitos superare fluctus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Quum iussus orbis totius</i> ARBITRO</l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Mactare</i> ISAACVM <i>non renuit</i> PATER:</l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Et mentis humana repellens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Sensa procul querulosque luctus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Nil esse duxit certius, optimus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Quam</i> REGIS ALMI <i>nutibus obsequi:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Vi cuius immensa sepulchro</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Vita redit revocata putri.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Munus probabis: cum placeant tibi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Quae scripta cultus egregios docent:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Quae iusta monstrant: Quae pudicas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Expoliunt</i> PIETATE <i>mentes.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Et fontis Vndas</i> CASTALII <i>&amp; specus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Lauru Virentes</i> AONIA <i>colus:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Castaque miraris choreas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">THESPIADVM, <i>resonosque cantus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Et celsa</i> PHOEBI <i>templa</i> PALVDIO</l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Ducente gaudes visere, nil pavens</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Rupes inaccessas, &amp; alti</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Terrificas</i> HELICONIS <i>umbras.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Hinc certioris praemia gloriae</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Quaerenda censens, perpetuum &amp; decus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29">
      <i>Quod falce</i> SATVRNVS <i>rapacis</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Quo[?]</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <notes>The right edge of the last line is cut off by the scan. The catchword at the bottom right is partly cut off; only "Quo" is visible. The reading "Vetus" in the first line and "quaque" are uncertain at this scan resolution. Stanza breaks are inferred from the lines and may not match the printed stanzas exactly.</notes>
